NESTED LOOPS

Nested loops are the capacity for loops to be ran inside of one another. For example:

A for loop can be ran inside of another for loop to have a separate count following the main one:

for(i=0;i<11;i++)
{
Console.WriteLine("Hi");
  for(p=0;p<=5;p++)
  {
    if(p%2==0)
    {
    Console.WriteLine("Bye");
    }
  }
}

This also works for do-while or while loops. Any number of nested loops can be added inside of a loop.
Beware! Any variable defined in the parent loop will NOT be able to be repeated inside any of its nested loops, parent loop variables takes priority over the offshoots.

